# Cloudflare Pages/Workers asset upload — excludes files from the deployed
# static site, same syntax and purpose as .gitignore but read by Cloudflare's
# deploy step specifically. Needed because Cloudflare's build environment
# auto-runs `npm install` when it sees package.json (this repo only has one
# for the optional Capacitor Android tooling — the deployed site itself has
# no build step, see README), and if the "build output directory" is left as
# the repo root, the resulting node_modules/ gets swept up as a deployable
# asset. That's what causes the "asset too large" error on
# node_modules/workerd/bin/workerd (Cloudflare's own deploy tooling, not a
# dependency of this project) — excluding node_modules/ here is the fix.
#
# The Android project and its own node_modules-equivalents are also
# irrelevant to the deployed web app and excluded for the same reason.
node_modules/
www/
android/
package.json
package-lock.json
.git/
